<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  launchd user agent for printkeeperd, the printkeeper daemon.

  This file is a TEMPLATE: every __HOME__ below must be substituted
  with your own home directory before installing it — launchd cannot
  expand "~" or "$HOME" inside ProgramArguments/StandardOutPath/
  StandardErrorPath itself, so this has to happen before the plist
  reaches launchctl. See packaging/darwin/README.md for the one-line
  command that does this and installs the result.

  ProgramArguments points at printkeeperd under this user's own
  Application Support directory, alongside everything else printkeeper
  already keeps there (the adopted-printer store, the IPC socket) — a
  location that never needs admin rights to write to, unlike
  /usr/local/bin. Whoever installs this is expected to have already put
  the built binary at that path; this plist does not build or copy it.

  RunAtLoad starts the daemon the moment it is bootstrapped (and again
  on every login), matching spec §6.6's "event-driven first... on
  daemon start". KeepAlive.SuccessfulExit=false means launchd restarts
  it after a crash (non-zero exit) but leaves it stopped after a clean,
  deliberate exit(0) — the standard idiom for a long-running agent that
  should come back from a crash without fighting a real shutdown.

  ThrottleInterval caps how often launchd will restart a crashing job:
  without it, a daemon that exits non-zero on every single start (a
  corrupted store, a permissions problem on its own directory) gets
  relaunched at launchd's own default cadence forever — exactly the
  "constant wakeups" anti-goal this whole daemon is framed around,
  left unguarded in the one failure mode most likely to produce it. 60
  seconds is generous enough that a genuine crash loop costs this
  machine almost nothing, while still recovering within a minute of
  whatever caused it being fixed.

  Nothing here raises a user notification on success or failure: spec's
  rule that a successful repair stays silent applies just as much to a
  daemon with no terminal as it does to the CLI, and the standard
  streams below only ever go to this agent's own log files, never to a
  visible UI.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>io.github.phpfc.printkeeper</string>

	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>__HOME__/Library/Application Support/printkeeper/bin/printkeeperd</string>
	</array>

	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>

	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<dict>
		<key>SuccessfulExit</key>
		<false/>
	</dict>

	<key>ThrottleInterval</key>
	<integer>60</integer>

	<key>ProcessType</key>
	<string>Background</string>

	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/printkeeper/agent.out.log</string>

	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/printkeeper/agent.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
